      "content": "To make it sound more authentic and relatable to inner-city areas or younger, more diverse demographics, consider the following revised version:\n\n\"Yo, what's good [Customer]? Sorry 'bout the delay, that's not what we promised. We gotchu - check yo' emails for the latest scoop on the shipment status. If it's still actin' up, let me know and I'll try to get the lowdown on what's really goin' on. We're all about gettin' ya the goods, ASAP. Keep it locked to your mailbox for the update.\"\n\nHowever, please note that using AAVE (African American Vernacular English) or other dialects requires sensitivity and an understanding of cultural nuances. Make sure your target audience appreciates the authenticity, and avoid stereotypes or tokenism. The goal is to establish rapport, not to perpetuate any negative or stigmatizing associations.",
      "source": "target",
